  topic: Board Discussion on Concussion Policy
  desc: Board members discussed Policy JJIF, with George Risch emphasizing the need
    for explicit parent/guardian involvement in return-to-play decisions and notification
    even when no concussion is suspected by school staff. Rosemarie DeAngelis and
    Claire Holman supported the idea of ensuring parents are fully informed about
    any concussion evaluations. The discussion highlighted the desire for clear communication
    and parental consent in all stages of concussion management.
  children:
  - seconds: 1872
    speaker: George Risch
    text: George Risch clarified that the 'accountants' mentioned in the finance report
      were actually 'auditors'. He then questioned the concussion policy, seeking
      assurance that parents would be part of the conversation regarding a child's
      return to play after a concussion, especially given potential long-term effects.
  - seconds: 2005
    speaker: Rosemarie DeAngelis
    text: Rosemarie DeAngelis confirmed the policy's intent was that if a parent did
      not want a child to return, they would not. She also supported the idea of parents
      being informed about any concussion evaluation, regardless of the outcome.
  - seconds: 2015
    speaker: George Risch
    text: George Risch further elaborated that the policy's current wording implied
      an internal assessment before medical referral, and he wanted explicit parent
      notification even if school staff deemed a medical visit unnecessary. He acknowledged
      the potential burden but stressed the importance of parental awareness.
  - seconds: 2084
    speaker: Ratliff
    text: Ratliff clarified that if the policy were sent back to committee, it would
      not be voted on tonight and would undergo further discussion at the next policy
      meeting before a second reading.
